74140280005.png"},"createdAt":"2025-08-26T00:04:13.178Z","lastActive":"2026-10-15T00:56:52.974Z","lvl":8,"status":"offline","id":"68acf9fdd1f45cb114023c5d","topMilestone":{"key":"creator.scripts","tier":10},"profile":{"url":"https://cdn.kocakz.me/images/945004edbf015f4d159dc5513379bab7b925e245534bb666559754af54056eaf.webp","original":"https://scriptblox.com/images/photo/68acf9fdd1f45cb114023c5d-1774140280005.png"}},"text":"@mjzt For certain games, that’s not true. This prevents your position from being updated to other players, but the server still sees your position. It’s useful for games like The Forge. A normal desync prevents both other players and the server from seeing your position. This one only prevents other players, so hitbox detectors still work.","parent":{"_id":"693dc055d9a0d1f6b305835c","commentBy":{"_id":"6939e189224649acf239b08e","username":"mjzt","profilePicture":"/images/photo/6939e189224649acf239b08e-1765401168407.jpg","status":"offline","id":"6939e189224649acf239b08e"},"text":"@wohoololskib all you people do is throw around the term desync, u can anchor ur hrp and some skid would call it desync. yea sure u could reset the character but itd do the same effect."},"edited":false,"likeCount":1,"dislikeCount":0,"createdAt":"2025-12-20T00:40:52.829Z","liked":false,"disliked":false}]}